    <DataNode elementId="GERANIOL" textLabel="geraniol" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="GLZPCOQZEFWAFX-JXMROGBWSA-N" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="200" centerY="500" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, nilo-poyanco">Natural essential oils contain monoterpenes as one of their major constituents. The oil accumulates in glands found in leaves, petals and trichomes. |FRAME: GERANIOL &quot;Geraniol&quot;| is an acyclic monoterpene alcohol that is found in the essential oils of many plant species, including nutmeg, |FRAME: TAX-94328| (ginger) |CITS: [11743782 ]|, |FRAME: TAX-39350| (basil) |CITS: [14657409]|, rosemary, sage, cardamom, grapefruit, and |FRAME: TAX-66014| (lemon grass) |CITS: [17230350]|. It is one of the three terpene compounds principally responsible for muscat aroma, and is emitted from flowers of many plant species with an intense rose scent. |FRAME: GERANIOL Geraniol| makes up to 86-98% of the essential oil in leaves of the camphor tree (|FRAME: TAX-192326|) |CITS: [15680985]|. |FRAME: GERANIOL &quot;Geraniol&quot;| has cancer antiproliferative properties due to its inhibitory effect on polyamine metabolism. It is known to decreases the activity of |FRAME: EC-4.1.1.17|, a key polyamine biosynthesis enzyme that is enhanced during cancer growth |CITS: [Carnesecchi01]|.</Comment>
